WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:02.560
After her breakout role on Gossip Girl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.240
Taylor Momsen gave up acting to sing&nbsp;
with her band The Pretty Reckless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.400
But you might not know what else she’s been&nbsp;
up to. Here's what she's been up to lately.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.120
Taylor Momsen entered the entertainment&nbsp;
industry at a very young age, well before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.040
she was old enough to make a decision about&nbsp;
it for herself. Throughout her career, Momsen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.960
has revealed that she had mixed feelings about&nbsp;
her upbringing. When asked about her childhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.400
Momsen would sometimes state that&nbsp;
becoming an actress was her choice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.480
and that her parents simply helped her find&nbsp;
opportunities, but later comments revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.480
a very different picture. For instance,&nbsp;
Momsen said in an interview with Revolver,

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.880
"My parents signed me up with Ford [Modeling]&nbsp;
at the age of two [...] No two-year-old wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.560
to be working, but I had no choice.&nbsp;
My whole life, I was in and out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:46.880
school. I didn't have friends. I was working&nbsp;
constantly and I didn't have a real life."

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.560
After moving to New York to film Gossip&nbsp;
Girl and finishing high school early,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.480
Momsen stated that while she loved her&nbsp;
parents, she was now legally responsible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.280
for herself and could enjoy more freedom and&nbsp;
independence. It seems like Momsen was pushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.430
into the spotlight before she was ready,&nbsp;
and now, her career is in her own hands.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.694
When Taylor Momsen landed the role of Jenny&nbsp;
Humphrey on Gossip Girl, it was her big break,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:17.826
"Are there skins on these almonds?  Fix it.  And in a timely fashion.  Otherwise you're all going as the Real Housewives of New Jersey for Halloween."  

00:01:17.826 --> 00:01:20.560
but some of the actors who worked&nbsp;
with her on the show weren't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.280
impressed behind the scenes. In later seasons,&nbsp;
Momsen was appearing on screen less and less,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.880
and Tim Gunn hinted at why this was&nbsp;
after guest starring on the show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.760
In an interview with E! News, Gunn, who had played&nbsp;
a mentor to Jenny on the series, said of Momsen,

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:37.440
"What a diva [...] She was pathetic, she&nbsp;
couldn't remember her lines, and she didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:41.600
even have that many. I thought to myself,&nbsp;
'Why are we being held hostage by this brat?'"

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:45.600
While the team behind Gossip Girl stated that&nbsp;
the airtime for Momsen's character was being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.000
cut for creative reasons, it seemed likely that&nbsp;
after working on the series for a few years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.440
Momsen was getting frustrated with&nbsp;
acting. Perhaps Gunn's characterization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.840
of her behavior on set was unfair, but&nbsp;
Momsen was definitely ready to move on.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.360
"Besides, I'm leaving like Blair wanted."

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:05.200
Although Momsen was a successful actress, she&nbsp;
had always secretly dreamed of making music,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.640
and after working on Gossip Girl,&nbsp;
she realized that she didn't enjoy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.400
being in front of the camera. She had been&nbsp;
writing her own songs since she was a child,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:15.840
and she wished she could start her own&nbsp;
band. One day, she realized that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.600
didn't have to act anymore if she didn't&nbsp;
want to. As Momsen told Cosmopolitan,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.080
"When I realized I could&nbsp;
actually make my decisions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.760
it was a very strange feeling. [...] It was&nbsp;
like, if I don't have to do this thing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.360
I don't enjoy doing anymore, or I don't&nbsp;
know if I ever really did, then I'm not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.240
gonna do it anymore! Because this is my life,&nbsp;
and I want to live it and enjoy it if I can."

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:37.811
She decided to focus on following&nbsp;
her passion for music instead.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:42.560
In her early years with The Pretty Reckless,&nbsp;
Taylor Momsen faced some obstacles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.960
Being a young woman in a male-dominated&nbsp;
genre, she wasn't always taken seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.280
but for a while, she tried to ignore the&nbsp;
phenomenon of sexism in the music industry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:55.280
She was branded as a "wild child" for her&nbsp;
onstage antics, and there were doubts about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.520
her authenticity as an artist. Later, she&nbsp;
realized that some of this criticism was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:04.134
aimed at her simply for being a teenage girl.&nbsp;
Momsen said in an interview with Louder Sound,

00:03:04.134 --> 00:03:08.080
"I was so in denial for so long about&nbsp;
sexism, but as I've gotten older I've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.080
realized it exists. [...] I've recognized&nbsp;
it more as I've gotten older that there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.840
a boys' club when it comes to rock 'n'&nbsp;
roll and it is a struggle to break into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.440
that and be accepted and treated with&nbsp;
the same respect as if you were a man."

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.800
Today, she's more comfortable&nbsp;
and confident in her own skin.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:27.422
"I am a female and I'm&nbsp;
psyched people are liking it."

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.480
Opening for Soundgarden in 2017 was one&nbsp;
of the highlights of Momsen's career.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:36.480
She never would have imagined that she would&nbsp;
appear at the same concert as Chris Cornell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.160
Soundgarden's lead vocalist and one&nbsp;
of her musical heroes. But tragedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.640
struck when Momsen received the news that&nbsp;
Cornell had died by suicide. She told SPIN,

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.080
"I was there that last night in&nbsp;
Detroit [...] I talked to him at night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.800
I gave him a hug and said goodbye. When I wake&nbsp;
up to that news the next morning [...] It just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:56.560
went from the most elating experience&nbsp;
to the one of the most devastating."

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.760
After a few more performances, Momsen decided to&nbsp;
put her own band's tour on hold. She explained,

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.040
"I couldn't grieve and continue to&nbsp;
get on stage every night and pretend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.670
put on this big rock show&nbsp;
like everything was okay."

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:12.640
Months after Chris Cornell's death, Taylor&nbsp;
Momsen and her bandmates were finally ready to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:16.960
start recording music again. But shortly after&nbsp;
they decided to begin working on a new album,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:21.520
Momsen got a heartbreaking phone call and&nbsp;
learned that their producer and her close friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:25.760
Kato Khandwala , had been killed in a&nbsp;
motorcycle accident. Momsen told Metro,

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.440
"He was so much more than a producer.&nbsp;
He was a fifth member of the band and my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.480
best friend in the world. I can't explain our&nbsp;
relationship but it was so immensely close."

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.040
After losing two people who meant so much to her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:40.640
Momsen tried to find a way to numb&nbsp;
her pain, and told The Daily Beast,

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:43.440
"I wouldn't say rock bottom, but I&nbsp;
was getting close to that [...] I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.560
was in this hole of depression&nbsp;
[...] and was not well mentally."

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:50.720
Momsen says that during this period of her life,&nbsp;
she did not want to engage with the outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:55.040
world at all, and she spent most of her time at&nbsp;
home. Rather than turning to others for help,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.808
she tried to isolate herself, even&nbsp;
though her bandmates lived nearby.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:02.640
In the midst of her grief, Taylor&nbsp;
Momsen found that even listening to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:06.320
music made her feel worse. The singer&nbsp;
explained to Illinois Entertainer,

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:10.000
"I got to a point where I couldn't listen&nbsp;
to music, and that was really sad for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.080
me. [...] If I put on any music — which has&nbsp;
always brought me such solace and hope and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.840
light — it would bring back some sort of&nbsp;
memory which was too much for me to handle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:22.000
or too painful, so I didn't have my outlet&nbsp;
which had always been there for me."

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.840
At the time, Momsen couldn't even bear the&nbsp;
thought of listening to her favorite artists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.000
let alone writing new songs. Eventually, she&nbsp;
began to pull herself out of her depression&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.440
by returning to her favorite band, The&nbsp;
Beatles. When she was able to listen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:37.885
to Soundgarden again, she knew it was&nbsp;
finally time to pick up her own guitar.

00:05:37.885 --> 00:05:42.080
Gossip Girl fans are getting excited&nbsp;
about an upcoming reboot of the series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:46.240
Naturally, the audience who tuned in for the&nbsp;
show's original run are wondering which cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.080
members might make an appearance. Fans of&nbsp;
Momsen who were introduced to her through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.360
Gossip Girl are wondering if she'll&nbsp;
be coming back for a guest appearance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:57.760
but the musician has no plans to return&nbsp;
to acting. Momsen told The Daily Beast,

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:01.840
"I don't have any plans to be any part of the&nbsp;
reboot. [...] I never really watched the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:06.240
when it was on the air. I don't really ever like&nbsp;
watching myself. It makes me uncomfortable."

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:10.160
However, Momsen is curious about how&nbsp;
the reboot will handle technology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:14.880
as the characters always had to have the latest&nbsp;
phones to spread gossip. She revealed that she's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.320
considering watching the reboot just to&nbsp;
see how the writers tackle this topic.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:23.600
There was a time when Taylor Momsen would reliably&nbsp;
pop up in the tabloids and gossip magazines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:28.320
but today, she has no real interest in chasing&nbsp;
fame. While she loves her career as a musician,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:32.400
she doesn't care to put her personal life&nbsp;
in the spotlight. Momsen revealed to People,

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.720
"Once there was paparazzi outside my door,&nbsp;
I learned very quickly to ignore all of it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:40.880
Fame is a fleeting thing, just something&nbsp;
that you have to deal with. It's not real."

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.040
She may not get as much media attention now&nbsp;
that her days on Gossip Girl are behind her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:48.960
but Momsen is happier with her career, so the&nbsp;
trade-off seems to have been worth it. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.717
while Momsen does use social media, she tries&nbsp;
not to spend too much time online in general.

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:58.000
After going silent for a few years, The&nbsp;
Pretty Reckless finally released their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:03.280
long-awaited fourth album on February&nbsp;
12, 2021. Titled Death by Rock and Roll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.520
Momsen says that although it might sound&nbsp;
morbid, the album sums up their philosophy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:11.600
on life. It’s a philosophy that late&nbsp;
producer Khandwala always celebrated:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:16.080
living according to your own terms. The album&nbsp;
topped the charts during the week of its release.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:19.120
"The fans are what make&nbsp;
it. We have the best fans."

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.440
With the loss of Khandwala, it took longer than&nbsp;
usual for the band to pull the album together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.720
and they had to figure out how they were&nbsp;
going to produce the album without him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:29.200
and who they should work&nbsp;
with instead. In addition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:34.320
the COVID-19 pandemic prompted the band to shift&nbsp;
the release date. Momsen told The Daily Beast,

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:38.640
"We finished the album right before COVID,&nbsp;
and due to the insane world circumstances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:40.000
we pushed it a little bit."

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.520
As soon as it's safe to do so, The Pretty&nbsp;
Reckless is ready to get back on the road,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:47.149
where you might be seeing a lot&nbsp;
more of Momsen in the coming years.

00:07:47.149 --> 00:08:01.300
If you or anyone you know is having suicidal thoughts, please call or chat online with the National Suicide Prevention Lifeline at 1-800-273-TALK (8255). Or Text HOME to the Crisis Text Line 741741.

